WEBVTT

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.940
I finally face Kai today.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:05.690
No, I'll be fighting Rei and
Takao down the line, too.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.420
I'm counting on you.
My new Bey, Draciel Gravity!

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:17.080
You've been hiding a
secret weapon all along, huh?

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:22.120
It just wasn't ready to
use in actual battles.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.050
I don't have the luxury of holding
back in this tournament.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.060
You should make
sure you're ready, too!

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.160
Kai is no ordinary Beyblader.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.640
No one's a match for me.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.480
What's gotten into him?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.820
Takao wasn't in
the last round.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.360
He's got a lot
of excess energy.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.960
I hope he doesn't go flying
off with all that energy!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.440
What?!

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.660
Big talk coming from you!

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.380
We know you play dirty!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.560
What was that?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.570
They're--!

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.760
It's Ralf and Johnny
from the European team!

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.730
What proof do you have to
make such a false claim?

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.500
False?!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.450
We haven't forgotten what you Barthez
Soldat guys did to us in the qualifiers!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.210
Why, whatever
could you mean?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.860
Let me spell it
out for you.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.530
I. Don't. Remember.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.810
I can't remember
every silly little thing!

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.580
Why you--

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.240
Not another step.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.120
Do you have any idea
what you're doing?!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.520
Is winning all that
matters to you?!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.320
Don't you have any
pride in your battles?!

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.340
What would you know?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.210
What?!

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.980
Winning is everything to us.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.780
No matter what it takes.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.370
No matter what
anyone says to us.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.960
I have nothing
more to say to you.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.320
Leave.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.970
Ralf...

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.730
Takao!

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:35.410
Like I said, we lost to
Barthez Soldat in the qualifiers.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:41.250
Yeah. I thought you guys would
represent Europe, so it was a huge shock.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.060
Luck can be
a factor in battle.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.810
I'm not here to
complain about that.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:49.140
But I take issue
with how we lost!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.900
How you lost?

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:57.700
They will stop at no low to inflict damage to their opponents.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:03.280
And not just in the stadium. Before our
match, our Beys were stolen and modded!

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.490
Even fires have broken
out in our waiting rooms!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.940
Guerrilla tactics...

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:13.660
And in the stadium,
illegal attacks await you!

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.740
What?!

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:21.840
Wait! If you know they're cheating,
you could appeal to the refs!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:27.920
Their tactics are so clever that we
didn't realize the truth until recently.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.440
That reminds me...

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.780
Something bothered me
about an earlier match...

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.410
What was that?

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.080
That's it! There!

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:45.100
I'll try playing back
the high-speed video!

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.830
Wow! You can see the tiniest details
of a Bey spinning that fast!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.570
Be quiet!

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.810
This is terrible...

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.720
So both Rei and you
guys got beat by this?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.560
No question about it!

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.700
Let's go take this memory
card to Chairman Daitenji!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.840
Yeah! If we bring the proof...

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.770
You're wasting your time.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.720
Illegal or not, it's the loser's fault
for not being good enough.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.860
What?!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:30.250
There's no guarantee that Barthez
Soldat would get disqualified, either.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.730
What did you say?

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.780
We have proof!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.800
He's probably right.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.130
No way! Why?!

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:42.640
Even if it were deemed
illegal, then what?

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:47.370
We can't go back to the qualifiers
and start everything over.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.340
I mean yeah, but...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:54.780
Yes, if that happened, the
tournament itself would fall apart.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.740
Ya see?

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:59.860
We've got a match
to get ready for.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.770
Just be careful!

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:09.560
I'm certain Barthez Soldat
pulled some dirty tricks on us, too.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.000
Max...

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:25.080
It's time for the second
match of the Spanish stage!

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.050
Today's stadium is...

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.890
Wow!

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:38.240
The Bull-Horn Stadium, equipped with 15,000 volt horns

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.160
that can send your Bey flying!

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.770
Go, Shoot!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:09.630
The first to challenge this stadium are the domineering Neo-Borg!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.840
Their opponents will be
the proud American heroes!

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.560
The PPB All Starz!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.490
They're really getting booed...

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:33.440
It'll be hard for Max and
Rick to fight like this...

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.520
A tough crowd, as usual.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:41.050
Silence!!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.120
Don't interfere in our battle!

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.820
Okay, Kai! I've been looking
forward to our battle!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.690
Kai...

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:11.250
The first battle will be Neo-Borg's Kai Hiwatari VS the PPB All Starz's Max Mizuhara!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.010
Come on, Kai!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.520
Here I come, Max!

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:27.650
Three! Two! One!

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.760
Go!

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.620
Well, well...

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.240
It's a wave.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.760
Draciel attacks are similar
to waves on a beach.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.360
A wave...

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:09.770
At first glance, it looks like
Dranzer has the upper hand,

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:16.370
but Draciel absorbs the hits and
releases them back like a wave.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:20.160
So it ebbs and flows?

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.240
Max is amazing!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:26.120
But Dranzer's attacks
are incredibly strong.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.290
How much of
this can it take?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:38.140
Not bad, Kai! I can't take
much more of those attacks.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.280
He's stubborn.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.730
I'll keep attacking until
the wave disperses!

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:46.320
Go, Dranzer Gigus!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:51.810
Becoming an all-consuming
tsunami, Draciel Gravity!

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.520
Burn, my Dranzer!!

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:11.930
Now!

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:12.880
What?!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:22.450
Our battle doesn't need
any tricks. Right, Kai?

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.860
Okay, Kai! Let's fight
fair and square!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:28.880
Bring it!

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.780
Pay attention!
This is their new strength!

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.000
You mean there's more?!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:45.970
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade G-Revolution"

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:55.110
Our battle doesn't need
any tricks. Right, Kai?

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.500
Okay, Kai! Let's fight
fair and square!

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.700
Bring it!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.060
Go, go, Draciel!

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:13.760
Engine Gear, full power!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.300
Gravity Control!

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:34.500
What's this?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.840
Engine Gear, release!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.560
Blazing Gig!

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.320
Draciel!

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:36.180
Draciel, Stadium Out!

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:40.880
Kai Hiwatari from
Neo-Borg wins the match!

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:52.740
That was one heck of a battle!

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:56.120
They were very evenly matched! The difference was paper thin!

00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:03.480
But if the rebound angle had been slightly
different, the winner may have been...

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:10.160
What kinda half-assed
battle was that?!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.620
Sorry! Guess my Bey
has a ways to go--

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:19.340
Why did you hold back that attack?
You call that fair play?!

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.810
You can say what you want,
but I fought my best!

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:28.050
It's a shame I lost,
but I'm proud of it!

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:32.090
Don't be stupid!
You mocked that battle!

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:37.800
I mocked that battle...?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:44.980
Time for the second battle!
From Neo-Borg, it's Yuriy Ivanov!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:49.930
From the PPB All Starz,
it's Rick Anderson!

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.620
What an exciting
battle that was.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:58.560
Is that what a world
level battle is like?

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:01.220
Yeah. And yet...

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.140
We've been...

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.380
Impossible!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:18.180
Wow! Rock Bison is pushing
Wolborg with its massive power!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.940
The end!

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.500
Wolborg, Stadium Out!

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:41.540
Yuriy loses after taking 15,000
volts straight to his Beyblade!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.010
Rick Anderson is the winner!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.290
I never thought Yuriy
would lose that way!

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:54.680
He might be
as strong as Kai!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.970
Who's gonna win?!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.420
I have no idea!

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:03.680
What's certain is that
the battle will be intense.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:08.040
In a head-on battle,
Kai's at a disadvantage.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:13.610
Kai'll pull through!
I just know he will!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:17.770
I got no time for
small fries! Get lost!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:22.840
Let me show you
what a real battle is!

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.700
It all ends on
the third battle!

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:35.140
Who will win? Neo-Borg?
Or the PPB All Starz?

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:40.760
Match two, third battle!
Kai Hiwatari VS Rick Anderson!

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.210
Ready? Three! Two! One!

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.620
Go, Shoot!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:53.300
Oh dear! Have Kai's
skills fallen behind?!

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:06.620
What? Does Kai still have
damage from our battle?

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:10.630
Rick is the kind of person
to take advantage of that!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.010
So this battle will...

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.240
That's not fair!

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.800
This is the cruelty of battle.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.890
If this keeps up...

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:24.060
No! Kai wouldn't
give up here!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.020
Well? You gonna
attack or not?

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.240
Then allow me!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:37.890
What?!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.060
That's--!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:44.530
Bastard!
You copied Max's move?!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.500
Wow, Kai!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.660
He's awesome!

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.050
I never thought he'd
use that to counter!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:55.880
That technique can help
him absorb damage!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.760
But Rick has
more power than Kai!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:03.210
Plus, I'm not sure how much longer
the balance type Dranzer can hold on...

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:13.570
Pathetic!
That won't work on me!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.330
Destroy him, Rock Bison!

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:22.080
The end!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.210
What?!

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:31.620
Rick!

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:34.880
Who do you
think Rock Bison is?!

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.330
He's nuts!

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:45.490
Incredible! He used the
electricity to send Dranzer flying!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.460
You're finished!

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.140
Drop Rock!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.600
Knock 'em flying!

00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:00.370
Blazing Gig!

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:04.800
Zan!

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.780
No!

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:23.300
Stadium Out!
The third battle is over!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:27.240
Kai from Neo-Borg
is the winner!

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:32.420
I lost?!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:41.920
It's only natural for a bull to
lose in a bull-fighting stadium.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:48.900
Kai's amazing! Only he could
pull off a technique like that!

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:54.240
Well look at that! He talked all that
trash but ended up losing anyway!

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:59.010
Obsessing over winning
is the wrong way to go!

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:03.200
I don't think his
style is wrong, either.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:08.520
Utilizing your opponent's
weakness isn't a bad thing!

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:12.730
It just means that Rick is
focused on the battle!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:17.760
That was just as awesome of
a battle as Kai and Max's!

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:23.050
We can't lose after watching
such an amazing battle!

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.340
Rick...

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:27.780
I lost.
Say whatever you want.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.490
No, I...

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.610
Not that I'm gonna listen.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:38.540
Don't give anything to the loser. That's the rule of battle.

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.680
The rule of battle...

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.100
Takao!

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:48.730
Do you truly intend to
battle against Barthez Soldat?

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:52.040
You don't know what
kind of tricks they'll pull.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:57.820
Did you see how cool their battle was?
We gotta be like that, too!

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:04.250
We can't win by default by
catching them in the act.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.600
You're darn right, Takao!

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:15.050
If they're gonna cheat, we'll just
knock 'em out with our fiery Beyspirits!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:21.540
In that case, we only
have one thing to say.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.290
Just win, Takao.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.980
Leave it to us!

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:29.420
Our Beyspirits
won't lose to cheaters!

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:59.420
I'm on fire!
Beybattles aren't games just to win!

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:01.810
Bladers aren't fighting machines!

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:08.150
I promised Ralf I'd wake them
up with my awesome Beyspirit!

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.380
But we're up against Barthez. I'm sure he's up to something.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.900
Keep your guard up, Takao!
Be careful, Daichi!

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.620
What?! No!

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:20.240
My Gaia Dragoon...!!
